title: "Conditional Sealing: a reference implementation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Baltes
    given-names: Simon
repository-code: "https://github.com/simbal21/conditional-sealing"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0-archive
date-released: "2026-10-01"
abstract: >-
  A reference implementation of conditional sealing, built between March and
  June 2026: data is encrypted once, its key is split 3-of-3 by Shamir secret
  sharing across three independent signing gates — a rented threshold network
  (Lit Protocol), a rented randomness/attestation network (drand or dcipher),
  and a refusal-only operator verifier — all locked behind a fourth gate, the
  chain, as the mandatory trigger holding no share; release happens only when
  a pre-agreed, chain-verified condition is met. Alongside the
  construction, the release documents a first-class negative result: a
  pre-committed, falsifiable six-condition demand instrument applied
  adversarially to 157 candidate companies found zero clean fits, and the
  project was retired on that evidence. Archived as a design record and
  reference — never externally audited, never run in production, with its
  on-chain components deployed to a public testnet only. The system was
  developed under the working name Cealis; the working name is preserved in
  the frozen specifications, audit records, and on-chain artifacts.
keywords:
  - conditional sealing
  - threshold cryptography
  - secret sharing
  - data escrow
  - smart contracts
  - timelock encryption
  - witness encryption
  - negative result
  - demand study
